78
00:04:34,050 --> 00:04:39,210
我希望你学完后对三件事形成清晰的认知：1.
What I want you to walk away with is a clear mental model of three things: 1.

79
00:04:39,890 --> 00:04:42,170
一个生产级语音智能体实际涉及什么。
What a production voice agent actually involves.

80
00:04:42,810 --> 00:04:45,795
2. 语音在你技术栈中的位置。以及 3，
2. Where voice belongs in your stack. And 3,

81
00:04:45,795 --> 00:04:49,610
我们从第 2 课开始将动手构建什么。
what we are going to build hands-on starting in Lesson 2.

82
00:04:50,330 --> 00:04:54,810
在深入架构之前，我想花一点时间谈谈为什么选择语音。
Before we get into the architecture, I want to spend a minute on why voice.

83
00:04:55,050 --> 00:04:59,043
为什么这很重要？有四个理由，让我们值得把它视为
Why does this matter? There are four reasons it's worth treating

84
00:04:59,043 --> 00:05:01,410
AI 时代的一等公民模态。
as a first class modality in the AI era.

85
00:05:01,730 --> 00:05:03,050
第一个原因最显而易见。
First one's the obvious one.

86
00:05:03,770 --> 00:05:06,070
语音是人类拥有的最自然交互界面。
Voice is the most natural interface humans have.

87
00:05:06,070 --> 00:05:08,650
我们人类已经说话了几十万年。
We've been talking for hundreds of thousands of years.

88
00:05:09,050 --> 00:05:11,030
打字只有几十年历史。
Typing's just a few decades old.

89
00:05:11,030 --> 00:05:14,330
所以语音是表达意图摩擦最低的方式。
So voice is the lowest friction way to express intent.

90
00:05:14,610 --> 00:05:16,730
无需菜单，无需表单，无需滚动。
No menus, no forms, no scrolling.

91
00:05:17,370 --> 00:05:20,739
第二个是副语言，这一点被低估了。
Second is paralanguage, and this one is underrated.

92
00:05:20,739 --> 00:05:25,410
一段语音话语携带的信息量远超同样的文本句子。
A voice utterance carries way more signal than the same sentence as text.

93
00:05:25,650 --> 00:05:30,343
它可能是语气、语速、犹豫、紧迫感、韵律、情绪，
It could be tone, pace, hesitation, urgency, prosody, emotion,

94
00:05:30,343 --> 00:05:35,210
那些能“听见”你的语意而不仅仅是你说了什么的智能体。
agents that can hear how you mean something, not just what you said.

95
00:05:35,410 --> 00:05:39,441
它们的行为与只读取文本的智能体截然不同。
They behave really differently from agents that just read your text.

96
00:05:39,441 --> 00:05:40,900
第三个是多模态。
Third is multimodality.

97
00:05:41,420 --> 00:05:44,913
语音不会取代你的 UI。它与 UI 配合使用。你说出意图。
Voice doesn't replace your UI. It pairs with it. You speak intent.

98
00:05:44,913 --> 00:05:46,500
你看到结构化的信息返回。
You see structured info back.

99
00:05:46,700 --> 00:05:51,660
最好的语音智能体会同时使用语音和 GUI。
The best voice agents are the ones that use voice and the GUI together.

100
00:05:52,380 --> 00:05:57,140
每种模态做自己最擅长的事。最后，第四个理由是无障碍性。
Each modality doing what it's best at. Finally, the fourth one is accessibility.

101
00:05:57,740 --> 00:06:02,599
语音能覆盖无法打字或无法阅读屏幕的用户，
Voice reaches users who cannot type or they can't read on the screen,

102
00:06:02,599 --> 00:06:04,730
无法导航复杂 GUI 的用户。
can't navigate a complex GUI.

103
00:06:05,010 --> 00:06:10,050
它通常是你能够交付的最无障碍的界面，这点很重要。
It's often the most accessible interface you can ship, and that matters.

104
00:06:10,530 --> 00:06:13,933
有了实时 AI，语音终于能够作为界面来工作，
With real-time AI, voice finally works as an interface

105
00:06:13,933 --> 00:06:16,050
并与你现有的 UI 搭配使用。
and paired with your existing UI.

106
00:06:16,330 --> 00:06:20,850
这会让产品体验发生阶跃式变化。那么让我来具体说明。
It's a step change in how products feel. So let me make that concrete.

107
00:06:21,660 --> 00:06:26,940
我们这里要用的一个例子是通过经典 GUI 预订航班。
One example that we are going to use here is booking a flight with a classic GUI.

108
00:06:27,340 --> 00:06:32,236
你会经历四个阶段。打开应用、搜索、选择日期，
You go through four phases. You open the app, you search, you pick dates,

109
00:06:32,236 --> 00:06:35,500
应用筛选条件，然后从选项中做出选择。
apply filters and then choose from the options.

110
00:06:35,580 --> 00:06:40,196
最后付款并确认。每个阶段都有自己的子任务。
And then finally pay and confirm. Every phase has its own subtask.

111
00:06:40,196 --> 00:06:42,760
总耗时很容易超过两分钟。
Total time easily over two minutes.

112
00:06:42,880 --> 00:06:44,360
而且你全程都在点击屏幕。
And you're tapping the entire time.

113
00:06:44,680 --> 00:06:48,148
现在想象用语音完成同一个任务，只需一句话，
Now imagine the same task on voice with a single utterance,

114
00:06:48,148 --> 00:06:51,120
帮我订一张下周五早上从 SF 到 NYC 的机票。
book me a flight from SF to NYC next Friday morning.

115
00:06:51,320 --> 00:06:54,240
智能体负责处理界面，你只需留在对话中。
The agent does the screens. You stay in the conversation.

116
00:06:54,880 --> 00:06:56,120
你可以直接口头确认。
You can confirm out loud.

117
00:06:56,720 --> 00:07:01,120
不到 10 秒就能完成。这里的重点不是语音会取代 GUI。
You'll be done in under 10 seconds. Now, the point isn't that voice replaces GUIs.

118
00:07:01,440 --> 00:07:05,400
重点是语音压缩了从意图到结果之间的摩擦。
The point is voice collapses the friction between intent and outcome.

119
00:07:05,760 --> 00:07:07,643
你会一再看到这种模式，
And you will see this pattern over

120
00:07:07,643 --> 00:07:10,400
在本课剩余部分的每个演示中一再出现。
and over in every demo for the rest of this lesson.

121
00:07:10,840 --> 00:07:14,240
那么，语音目前真正被用在哪里？下一步又会走向何方？
So where is voice actually being used today and where is it going next?

122
00:07:14,560 --> 00:07:19,200
整个画面是一张大图，我称之为语音智能体宇宙。
This whole scene is one big picture, what I call the voice agent universe.

123
00:07:19,480 --> 00:07:22,560
我们将一个气泡一个气泡地把它填满。
And we are going to fill it one bubble at a time.

124
00:07:22,800 --> 00:07:26,775
如果你在过去几年里听说过语音 AI，
So if you've heard about voice AI over the last couple of years,

125
00:07:26,775 --> 00:07:32,278
相关背景几乎一定是联络中心：支持、IVR、智能体辅助、通话质检，
the context was almost certainly the contact center: support, IVR, agent assist, call QA,

126
00:07:32,278 --> 00:07:34,800
也就是右侧那个橙色集群。
that's the orange cluster on the right.

127
00:07:35,160 --> 00:07:39,188
经济效益清晰，工作流受限，买家已经存在，
Economics are clear, workflows are constrained, the buyers exist,

128
00:07:39,188 --> 00:07:41,520
这就是行业从那里起步的原因。
that's why the industry started there.

129
00:07:41,680 --> 00:07:44,619
但那只是语音真正归属场景中的一小块。
But that's a tiny slice of where voice actually belongs.

130
00:07:44,619 --> 00:07:47,120
更大的图景是这个宇宙的其余部分。
The bigger picture is the rest of this universe.

131
00:07:47,680 --> 00:07:51,880
语音作为每个行业、每种软件中的一项功能。
Voice as a feature of every kind of software across every industry.

132
00:07:52,290 --> 00:07:54,894
金融科技中，语音作为你账户的界面，
Fintech, voice as the interface to your account,

133
00:07:54,894 --> 00:07:58,070
作为你投资组合的界面；也可能在车内，原因显而易见——
to your portfolio, or it could be in-car for the obvious reason

134
00:07:58,070 --> 00:08:00,610
因为你不能把手从方向盘上移开。
because you can't take your hands off the wheel.

135
00:08:00,890 --> 00:08:05,798
以医疗健康为例，可以有临床听写等用例，
Take healthcare for example, you can have use cases like clinical dictation,

136
00:08:05,798 --> 00:08:08,290
患者登记、签到，凡是你说得出的。
patient intake, check-ins, you name it.

137
00:08:08,410 --> 00:08:12,420
也可能是开发工具、可以真正对话的编码助手，
It could be dev tools, coding assistants you can actually talk to,

138
00:08:12,420 --> 00:08:16,430
当然还有面向无法轻松使用 GUI 用户的辅助功能。
and obviously accessibility for users who can't easily use a GUI.

