00:11:39,200 --> 00:11:39,640
好的。
All right.

195
00:11:39,840 --> 00:11:42,751
如今语音 AI 基本上有两种架构
There are essentially two architectures in voice AI today

196
00:11:42,751 --> 00:11:45,840
而它们之间存在一个没人愿意做出的权衡。
and there's a trade-off between them that nobody wants to make.

197
00:11:46,600 --> 00:11:50,760
第一种是级联式设置，这是经典技术栈。
First one is your cascaded setup. It's the classic stack.

198
00:11:51,720 --> 00:11:55,034
你先有语音转文字，然后有你的 LLM，
You have speech to text, then you have your LLM,

199
00:11:55,034 --> 00:11:58,000
最后再是文字转语音。
and then you finally have text to speech.

200
00:11:58,320 --> 00:12:02,833
你可能还需要深度推理，因为当你原样使用完整的 LLM 技术栈时，
You might also need deep reasoning because as you are using your full LLM stack as is,

201
00:12:02,833 --> 00:12:03,880
它很容易调试。
it is easy to debug.

202
00:12:04,200 --> 00:12:08,653
每一步都是文本，但每一轮的延迟会达到 1 到 3 秒，
Every step is text, but the latency is going to be 1 to 3 seconds per turn,

203
00:12:08,653 --> 00:12:12,200
端到端，这对实时语音智能体来说并不理想。
end to end, which is not ideal for a real time voice agent.

204
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:16,563
而且语音转文字会去掉语气、情绪、节奏，
And speech to text strips out the tone, the emotion, the pacing,

205
00:12:16,563 --> 00:12:17,840
所有副语言信息。
all the paralanguage.

206
00:12:17,840 --> 00:12:21,000
在你的智能体看到输入之前，你已经丢失了所有这些信号。
You lose all of that signal before your agent ever sees the input.

207
00:12:21,470 --> 00:12:25,696
第二种是实时架构，也就是语音到语音模型，
Second one is a real time architecture, aka voice to voice models,

208
00:12:25,696 --> 00:12:29,230
输入是语音，输出也是语音。
where the input is speech and the output is also speech.

209
00:12:30,030 --> 00:12:35,670
而且只有一个模型，延迟降到 200 到 500 毫秒。
And there's this one single model, the latency drops to 200 to 500 milliseconds.

210
00:12:35,790 --> 00:12:37,190
这才是你想要的延迟水平。
That's the kind of latency you want.

211
00:12:37,310 --> 00:12:40,558
模型能听到语气、音高、犹豫、情绪，
The model hears tone, pitch, hesitation, emotion,

212
00:12:40,558 --> 00:12:44,940
所有那些我们在级联式技术栈中丢失的副语言信号。
all the paralinguistic signals that we lost with the cascaded stack.

213
00:12:45,620 --> 00:12:48,540
但你确实会失去对 LLM 技术栈的访问。
But you do lose access to your LLM stack.

214
00:12:49,100 --> 00:12:53,005
这里的大脑是通用模型，把它与你的 RAG、你的工具连接起来，
The brain here is generic wiring it up with your RAG, with your tools,

215
00:12:53,005 --> 00:12:56,020
与你的领域知识连接起来并不简单。
with your domain knowledge is not straightforward.

216
00:12:56,540 --> 00:13:01,460
所以你必须二选一：要么获得低延迟，要么获得深度推理。
So you have to pick one. Either you get low latency or you get deep reasoning.

217
00:13:01,900 --> 00:13:05,380
要么获得自然度，要么利用你现有的“大脑”。
Either you get naturalness or you can leverage your existing brain.

218
00:13:06,160 --> 00:13:08,160
这就是那个没人愿意做出的权衡。
That is the trade-off nobody wants to make.

219
00:13:08,360 --> 00:13:12,952
因此 Vocal Bridge 的答案，是我们所谓的“礼宾式架构”，
So Vocal Bridge's answer is what we call the concierge architecture,

220
00:13:12,952 --> 00:13:16,040
一个处理对话的实时大脑。
a real time brain that handles a conversation.

221
00:13:16,440 --> 00:13:19,677
比如填充词、话轮转换、副语言
So things like fillers, turn taking, paralanguage

222
00:13:19,677 --> 00:13:21,809
它只会在需要深度推理时委派给你的 LLM
and it only delegates to your LLM

223
00:13:21,809 --> 00:13:26,388
或者需要执行专项任务时
when it needs deep reasoning or it needs to execute a specialized task

224
00:13:26,388 --> 00:13:30,020
也就是你的 LLM 或智能体工作流真正擅长的事情。
that your LLM or your agentic workflow is really good at.

225
00:13:30,230 --> 00:13:34,830
这样你既能获得实时延迟，现有的 LLM 技术栈也保持完整。
So you get real time latency and your existing LLM stack stays intact.

226
00:13:35,190 --> 00:13:37,723
具体实现是我们的秘诀，
The implementation is really our secret sauce,

227
00:13:37,723 --> 00:13:40,510
但高层形态就是你在屏幕上看到的。
but the high level shape is what you see on the screen.

228
00:13:41,470 --> 00:13:45,910
这就是你在进入第 2 课之前应该掌握的架构图景。
That's the architectural picture you should walk into Lesson 2 with.

